 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "You flip a coin 144 times and count the number of heads.\n",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 528641,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What is the mean of the corresponding distribution?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Since the number of heads is distributed normally, it can be shown that the mean of <i>n</i> flips is <span data-math=\"\\frac{n}{2}\"></span>and the standard deviation is <span data-math=\"\\frac{{\\sqrt n }}{2}\"></span> as long as <span data-math=\"n \\geq {\\text{ }}20\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Since <i>n</i> is 144, <span data-math=\"\\frac{n}{2}\"></span> is 72.</p>\n<p>The mean is 72.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "72\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 528642,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What is the standard deviation of the corresponding distribution?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Since the number of heads is distributed normally, it can be shown that the mean of <i>n</i> flips is <span data-math=\"\\frac{n}{2}\"></span>and the standard deviation is <span data-math=\"\\frac{{\\sqrt n }}{2}\"></span> as long as <span data-math=\"n \\geq {\\text{ }}20\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Since <i>n</i> is 144, <span data-math=\"\\frac{{\\sqrt n }}{2} = \\frac{{\\sqrt {144} }}{2} = \\frac{{12}}{2} = 6\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The standard deviation is 6.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "6"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 528643,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "You flipped 81 heads. At what percentile does that fall?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Since the number of heads is distributed normally, it can be shown that the mean of <i>n</i> flips is <span data-math=\"\\frac{n}{2}\"></span>and the standard deviation is <span data-math=\"\\frac{{\\sqrt n }}{2}\"></span> as long as <span data-math=\"n \\geq {\\text{ }}20\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Since <i>n</i> is 144, <span data-math=\"\\frac{n}{2}\"></span> is 72.</p>\n<p>The mean is 72.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{\\sqrt n }}{2} = \\frac{{\\sqrt {144} }}{2} = \\frac{{12}}{2} = 6\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The standard deviation is 6.</p>\n<p>In an empty cell of Google Sheets, use the function NORM.DIST.</p>\n<p>NORM.DIST(your data value, your mean, your standard deviation, TRUE)</p>\n<p>Your data value is 81, your mean is 72, and your standard deviation is 6.</p>\n<p>Using your data: =NORM.DIST(81, 72, 6,TRUE)</p>\n<p>You will see the decimal version of the percentile: 0.9331927987</p>\n<p>Convert the decimal to an approximate percentage: the 93<sup>rd</sup> percentile</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "93<sup>rd</sup>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
